# Vacuum — packages to keep OUT of the image, even when something depends
# on them. Passed to mklive's -g. Empty by default.
#
# This is the knob for shrinking the ISO. The image is dominated by things
# that cost disk but no memory, so trimming here changes download size and
# nothing else about how the running desktop feels:
#
#   wifi-firmware      several hundred MB of vendor blobs, pulled in by
#                      base-system. Dropping it roughly halves the ISO and
#                      leaves most laptops with no working Wi-Fi, which is
#                      a bad trade for an image whose job is to install
#                      itself onto unknown hardware. Uncomment only if you
#                      know the target machine's network card is supported
#                      by an in-tree driver, or you will install over
#                      ethernet.
#   memtest86+         a boot menu entry, ~2 MB.
#   dejavu-fonts-ttf   ~7 MB; leaves nothing but bitmap fonts, so tint2 and
#                      GTK lose their typeface.
#
# Uncomment to apply:
# wifi-firmware
# memtest86+
